{"chapter": "morphisms", "node_kind": "section_title", "parent_tag": "01TZ", "placeholders": {}, "render": {"prefix": "\\section{", "suffix": "}\n\\label{section-open}"}, "risk_level": "R1", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:5420edd28f396a4426d58d375eb79af6da2eba5d267a24e275279a7349f0a3b7", "source_text": "Open morphisms", "source_text_hash": "sha256:43252e9b87b39a04cd511244589a48977040b451ad93c3f3b410e9af91959631", "unit_id": "tag:01TZ:title"}
{"chapter": "morphisms", "node_kind": "definition", "parent_tag": "01TZ", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$f : X \\to S$", "MATH_0002": "$f$", "MATH_0003": "$f$", "MATH_0004": "$S' \\to S$", "MATH_0005": "$f' : X_{S'} \\to S'$", "STRUCT_0001": "\\begin{enumerate}", "STRUCT_0002": "\\item", "STRUCT_0003": "\\item", "STRUCT_0004": "\\end{enumerate}", "TEXTITCLOSE_0001": "}", "TEXTITCLOSE_0002": "}", "TEXTITOPEN_0001": "{\\it ", "TEXTITOPEN_0002": "{\\it "}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{definition}\n\\label{definition-open}\n", "suffix": "\\end{definition}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:c02fafbfdac58594863bdf31f2d0d08e200568022b597ee066b29f533465cfce", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:a2dd84d548b4fea9af581da59832641ad0ad88af5a96e14a6e5a858be7c5311f", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a morphism.\n<STRUCT_0001>\n<STRUCT_0002> We say <MATH_0002> is <TEXTITOPEN_0001>open<TEXTITCLOSE_0001> if the map on underlying\ntopological spaces is open.\n<STRUCT_0003> We say <MATH_0003> is <TEXTITOPEN_0002>universally open<TEXTITCLOSE_0002> if for any morphism of\nschemes <MATH_0004> the base change <MATH_0005> is open.\n<STRUCT_0004>\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:a85c20ef03d9bfa2e97bb912e6b051f8175f7f6ad54828d4e253c11db431ebd0", "unit_id": "tag:01U0:statement"}
{"chapter": "morphisms", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "01TZ", "placeholders": {"REF_0001": "\\ref{topology-lemma-closed-open-map-specialization}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{lemma-open-generizing}", "REF_0003": "\\ref{lemma-generalizations-lift-flat}", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:37aa537a045be2335927bf33dffb42ab43bb18e5890854b461794b6101ec2d95", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nAccording to\nTopology, Lemma <REF_0001>\ngeneralizations lift along certain types of open maps of topological\nspaces. In fact generalizations lift along any open morphism of schemes\n(see\nLemma <REF_0002>).\nAlso, we will see that generalizations lift along flat morphisms\nof schemes (Lemma <REF_0003>).\nThis sometimes in turn implies that the morphism is open.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:0f8258a6055e426cf7e219eff2db4d7f113ddcf3472457c0daee6f5512a52695", "unit_id": "tag:01TZ:prose-0001"}
{"chapter": "morphisms", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "01TZ", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$f : X \\to S$", "MATH_0002": "$f$", "MATH_0003": "$f$", "MATH_0004": "$f$", "MATH_0005": "$f$", "MATH_0006": "$f$", "MATH_0007": "$f$", "STRUCT_0001": "\\begin{enumerate}", "STRUCT_0002": "\\item", "STRUCT_0003": "\\item", "STRUCT_0004": "\\end{enumerate}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-locally-finite-presentation-universally-open}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:40d36eb94f91301986c98b48a96a351e5d4598e4bf0044b79b2a172f5066b43c", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:bc3f9ed7a433402e3cd17933a6fecb8d3d68c56f6138625f5ee9c1d0a327f784", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a morphism.\n<STRUCT_0001>\n<STRUCT_0002> If <MATH_0002> is locally of finite presentation and generalizations lift\nalong <MATH_0003>, then <MATH_0004> is open.\n<STRUCT_0003> If <MATH_0005> is locally of finite presentation and generalizations lift\nalong every base change of <MATH_0006>, then <MATH_0007> is universally open.\n<STRUCT_0004>\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:8b2c61985c0b7e501b1fba4996909b885d4d00bc7741f8fc9034f6bae5913786", "unit_id": "tag:01U1:statement"}
{"chapter": "morphisms", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "01TZ", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$X$", "MATH_0002": "$S$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{algebra-lemma-going-up-down-specialization}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{algebra-proposition-fppf-open}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:d370a34d7f00ffbf05a1092daf73f9253c7c18d61d8150fef6a4b4fd9e1f5bb0", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:b94deca6fd5fe708b7e630ab9da7fa272125e794a0aee1860938f7bbbc2ed697", "source_text": "It suffices to prove the first assertion.\nThis reduces to the case where both <MATH_0001> and <MATH_0002> are affine.\nIn this case the result follows from\nAlgebra, Lemma <REF_0001>\nand Proposition <REF_0002>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:27017f0ed014216e5e6ac282203307a96c9952e2add3a0fa42f8edf03af0367d", "unit_id": "tag:01U1:proof"}
{"chapter": "morphisms", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "01TZ", "placeholders": {"REF_0001": "\\ref{lemma-fppf-open}", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:8108f031bc28310357d8d3ba7ac31921d95e9488efb70eb28905af44cec48445", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nSee also Lemma <REF_0001> for the case of a morphism\nflat of finite presentation.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:b9ab21163e735f07f605582f869af4041dc761728efe28e463d3234ab6fe966d", "unit_id": "tag:01TZ:prose-0002"}
